IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ccc-core`
IMPORT `ccc29-xxvii-a-interpretation-penalty`
IMPORT `ccc29-xxviii-3-peace-810-21`

-- ccc29-tests-xxviii-3-peace-810-21.l4 -- tests for sections 810.21 to 811.1 of the Criminal Code (Canada).
-- Every expected value is written from the text before the run, beside its assertion. Argument order is the GIVEN order of each function.

§ `Tests -- section 810.21`

-- "any of sections 83.3 and 810 to 810.2": 83.3 is in; 810 and 810.2 are the ends of the range and are in; 810.01, 810.011, 810.02, 810.03 and 810.1 lie between them in the Code's order and are in; 810.21 and 810.3 are after 810.2; 83.2 and 83.31 are not 83.3.
#ASSERT `s 810.21(1) the section is one of 83.3 and 810 to 810.2` 83.3 EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 810.21(1) the section is one of 83.3 and 810 to 810.2` 810 EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 810.21(1) the section is one of 83.3 and 810 to 810.2` 810.01 EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 810.21(1) the section is one of 83.3 and 810 to 810.2` 810.011 EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 810.21(1) the section is one of 83.3 and 810 to 810.2` 810.02 EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 810.21(1) the section is one of 83.3 and 810 to 810.2` 810.03 EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 810.21(1) the section is one of 83.3 and 810 to 810.2` 810.1 EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 810.21(1) the section is one of 83.3 and 810 to 810.2` 810.2 EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 810.21(1) the section is one of 83.3 and 810 to 810.2` 810.21 EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 810.21(1) the section is one of 83.3 and 810 to 810.2` 810.3 EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 810.21(1) the section is one of 83.3 and 810 to 810.2` 809 EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 810.21(1) the section is one of 83.3 and 810 to 810.2` 83.2 EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 810.21(1) the section is one of 83.3 and 810 to 810.2` 83.31 EQUALS FALSE
-- 810.21(1): (the section, the prosecutor applies).
#ASSERT `s 810.21(1) a provincial court judge may order that the defendant appear by audioconference or videoconference` 810 TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 810.21(1) a provincial court judge may order that the defendant appear by audioconference or videoconference` 83.3 TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 810.21(1) a provincial court judge may order that the defendant appear by audioconference or videoconference` 810 FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 810.21(1) a provincial court judge may order that the defendant appear by audioconference or videoconference` 811 TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 810.21(1) a provincial court judge may order that the defendant appear by audioconference or videoconference` 811 FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 810.21(2) sections 714.1 to 714.8 and Part XXII.01 apply to the proceedings` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 810.21(2) sections 714.1 to 714.8 and Part XXII.01 apply to the proceedings` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Tests -- section 810.22`

-- 810.22(1): (section of the order, becomes resident elsewhere, charged etc. elsewhere, a peace officer applies, the Attorney General applies).
#ASSERT `s 810.22(1) a provincial court judge may transfer the order to a provincial court judge in the other territorial division` 810 TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 810.22(1) a provincial court judge may transfer the order to a provincial court judge in the other territorial division` 810.1 FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 810.22(1) a provincial court judge may transfer the order to a provincial court judge in the other territorial division` 83.3 TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 810.22(1) a provincial court judge may transfer the order to a provincial court judge in the other territorial division` 810 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 810.22(1) a provincial court judge may transfer the order to a provincial court judge in the other territorial division` 810 FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 810.22(1) a provincial court judge may transfer the order to a provincial court judge in the other territorial division` 811 TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- 810.22(2): (not in the same province, the provincial AG consents, the information was laid with the AG of Canada's consent, the AG of Canada consents). The answer is "barred for want of consent".
#ASSERT `s 810.22(2) the transfer is barred for want of the consent that the subsection requires` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 810.22(2) the transfer is barred for want of the consent that the subsection requires` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 810.22(2) the transfer is barred for want of the consent that the subsection requires` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 810.22(2) the transfer is barred for want of the consent that the subsection requires` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 810.22(2) the transfer is barred for want of the consent that the subsection requires` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 810.22(2) the transfer is barred for want of the consent that the subsection requires` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 810.22(2) the transfer is barred for want of the consent that the subsection requires` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 810.22(2) the transfer is barred for want of the consent that the subsection requires` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- 810.22(3): (the judge is unable to act, the other judge is of the same court).
#ASSERT `s 810.22(3) the powers of the judge in relation to the order may be exercised by another judge of the same court` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 810.22(3) the powers of the judge in relation to the order may be exercised by another judge of the same court` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 810.22(3) the powers of the judge in relation to the order may be exercised by another judge of the same court` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Tests -- section 810.3`

-- 810.3(1): the eight matters; another matter is not named; outside the listed sections.
#ASSERT `s 810.3(1) the authority is required to designate or specify the matter` TRUE `s 810.3(1)(a) designate the persons or classes of persons that may take samples of bodily substances` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 810.3(1) the authority is required to designate or specify the matter` TRUE `s 810.3(1)(b) designate the places or classes of places at which the samples are to be taken` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 810.3(1) the authority is required to designate or specify the matter` TRUE `s 810.3(1)(c) specify the manner in which the samples are to be taken` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 810.3(1) the authority is required to designate or specify the matter` TRUE `s 810.3(1)(d) specify the manner in which the samples are to be analyzed` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 810.3(1) the authority is required to designate or specify the matter` TRUE `s 810.3(1)(e) specify the manner in which the samples are to be stored, handled and destroyed` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 810.3(1) the authority is required to designate or specify the matter` TRUE `s 810.3(1)(f) specify the manner in which the records of the results of the analysis of the samples are to be protected and destroyed` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 810.3(1) the authority is required to designate or specify the matter` TRUE `s 810.3(1)(g) designate the persons or classes of persons that may destroy the samples` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 810.3(1) the authority is required to designate or specify the matter` TRUE `s 810.3(1)(h) designate the persons or classes of persons that may destroy the records of the results of the analysis of the samples` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 810.3(1) the authority is required to designate or specify the matter` TRUE `s 810.3(1) another matter` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 810.3(1) the authority is required to designate or specify the matter` FALSE `s 810.3(1)(a) designate the persons or classes of persons that may take samples of bodily substances` EQUALS NOTHING
-- 810.3(2).
#ASSERT `s 810.3(2) the authority may make the designation` `s 810.3(2)(a) designate the persons or classes of persons to make a demand for a sample of a bodily substance` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 810.3(2) the authority may make the designation` `s 810.3(2)(b) designate the persons or classes of persons to specify the regular intervals at which a defendant must provide a sample` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 810.3(2) the authority may make the designation` `s 810.3(2) another designation` EQUALS NOTHING
-- 810.3(3): (the samples are those referred to, dealt with in accordance with the designations).
#ASSERT `s 810.3(3) the taking, analysis, storage, handling or destruction of the sample, or the protection or destruction of the record, is barred` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 810.3(3) the taking, analysis, storage, handling or destruction of the sample, or the protection or destruction of the record, is barred` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 810.3(3) the taking, analysis, storage, handling or destruction of the sample, or the protection or destruction of the record, is barred` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- 810.3(4): (provided under a recognizance, reasonably expected to be used as evidence in a proceeding for an offence under section 811).
#ASSERT `s 810.3(4) the authority is required to cause the samples to be destroyed within the period prescribed by regulation` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 810.3(4) the authority is required to cause the samples to be destroyed within the period prescribed by regulation` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 810.3(4) the authority is required to cause the samples to be destroyed within the period prescribed by regulation` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- 810.3(6): the notice; the first sample no earlier than 24 hours after service; later samples at regular intervals of at least seven days.
#ASSERT `s 810.3(6) the notice is required to specify the places and times at which and the days on which the defendant must provide samples` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 810.3(6) the notice is required to specify the places and times at which and the days on which the defendant must provide samples` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 810.3(6) the first sample is barred because it is taken earlier than 24 hours after the defendant is served with the notice` 23 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 810.3(6) the first sample is barred because it is taken earlier than 24 hours after the defendant is served with the notice` 24 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 810.3(6) the first sample is barred because it is taken earlier than 24 hours after the defendant is served with the notice` 25 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 810.3(6) the subsequent samples are taken at regular intervals of at least seven days` 7 TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 810.3(6) the subsequent samples are taken at regular intervals of at least seven days` 6 TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 810.3(6) the subsequent samples are taken at regular intervals of at least seven days` 7 FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 810.3(6) the subsequent samples are taken at regular intervals of at least seven days` 8 TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE

§ `Tests -- section 810.4`

-- 810.4(1): (provided under a recognizance, used for the purpose of determining compliance).
#ASSERT `s 810.4(1) the use of the bodily substance is barred` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 810.4(1) the use of the bodily substance is barred` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 810.4(1) the use of the bodily substance is barred` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- 810.4(2): (the results are those referred to, subsection (3) allows the use or disclosure).
#ASSERT `s 810.4(2) the use or disclosure of the results of the analysis is barred` TRUE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 810.4(2) the use or disclosure of the results of the analysis is barred` TRUE NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 810.4(2) the use or disclosure of the results of the analysis is barred` TRUE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 810.4(2) the use or disclosure of the results of the analysis is barred` FALSE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- 810.4(3): (the use, the results are made anonymous).
#ASSERT `s 810.4(3) the results may be disclosed or used` `s 810.4(3) disclosure to the defendant to whom the results relate` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 810.4(3) the results may be disclosed or used` `s 810.4(3) use or disclosure in the course of an investigation of an offence under section 811` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 810.4(3) the results may be disclosed or used` `s 810.4(3) use or disclosure in a proceeding for an offence under section 811` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 810.4(3) the results may be disclosed or used` `s 810.4(3) use or disclosure for statistical or other research purposes` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 810.4(3) the results may be disclosed or used` `s 810.4(3) use or disclosure for statistical or other research purposes` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 810.4(3) the results may be disclosed or used` `s 810.4(3) another use or disclosure` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- 810.4(4): guilty if the person contravenes (1) or (2); the answers of (1) and (2) are inputs here.
#ASSERT `s 810.4(4) the person is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction` (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 810.4(4) the person is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction` (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 810.4(4) the person is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction` (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 810.4(4) the person is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction` NOTHING (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 810.4(4) the person is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction` (JUST FALSE) NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`s 810.4(4) the punishment for the offence`'s `maximum fine`) EQUALS (`a fine of` 5000)
#ASSERT (`s 810.4(4) the punishment for the offence`'s `maximum imprisonment`) EQUALS (`imprisonment for a term of` `two years less a day`)
#ASSERT (`s 810.4(4) the punishment for the offence`'s `mode`) EQUALS `on summary conviction`

§ `Tests -- sections 810.5, 811 and 811.1`

-- 810.5(1).
#ASSERT `s 810.5(1) sections 486 to 486.5 and 486.7 apply to the proceedings` 810.02 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 810.5(1) sections 486 to 486.5 and 486.7 apply to the proceedings` 83.3 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 810.5(1) sections 486 to 486.5 and 486.7 apply to the proceedings` 811 EQUALS NOTHING
-- 810.5(2): (the provision of the order, made in proceedings referred to in (1), the person fails to comply).
#ASSERT `s 810.5(2) the person is guilty of an offence under section 486.6` (`Provision of the Code` OF 486.4, "(1)") TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 810.5(2) the person is guilty of an offence under section 486.6` (`Provision of the Code` OF 486.4, "(2)") TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 810.5(2) the person is guilty of an offence under section 486.6` (`Provision of the Code` OF 486.4, "(3)") TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 810.5(2) the person is guilty of an offence under section 486.6` (`Provision of the Code` OF 486.5, "(1)") TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 810.5(2) the person is guilty of an offence under section 486.6` (`Provision of the Code` OF 486.5, "(2)") TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 810.5(2) the person is guilty of an offence under section 486.6` (`Provision of the Code` OF 486.4, "(1)") TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 810.5(2) the person is guilty of an offence under section 486.6` (`Provision of the Code` OF 486.4, "(1)") FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 810.5(2) the person is guilty of an offence under section 486.6` (`Provision of the Code` OF 486.5, "(3)") TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 810.5(2) the person is guilty of an offence under section 486.6` (`Provision of the Code` OF 486.1, "(1)") TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- 811: (the section of the recognizance, the person commits a breach).
#ASSERT `s 811 the person is guilty of an offence` 810 TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 811 the person is guilty of an offence` 810.03 TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 811 the person is guilty of an offence` 83.3 TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 811 the person is guilty of an offence` 810.2 FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 811 the person is guilty of an offence` 810.21 TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 811 the class of the offence` EQUALS `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`
#ASSERT (`s 811(a) the punishment on indictment`'s `mode`) EQUALS `by indictment`
#ASSERT (`s 811(a) the punishment on indictment`'s `maximum imprisonment`) EQUALS (`imprisonment for a term of` (`Length of time` OF 4, 0, 0, FALSE))
#ASSERT (`s 811(a) the punishment on indictment`'s `maximum fine`) EQUALS `no fine is stated`
#ASSERT (`s 811(b) the punishment on summary conviction`'s `mode`) EQUALS `on summary conviction`
#ASSERT (`s 811(b) the punishment on summary conviction`'s `maximum imprisonment`) EQUALS (`imprisonment for a term of` `two years less a day`)
-- 811.1(1): (a prosecution for breach of a no-consumption condition, the certificate purports to be signed by an analyst, it states the analysis and its result).
#ASSERT `s 811.1(1) the certificate is admissible in evidence` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 811.1(1) the certificate is admissible in evidence` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 811.1(1) the certificate is admissible in evidence` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 811.1(1) the certificate is admissible in evidence` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- proof of the statements: (the certificate is admissible, evidence to the contrary).
#ASSERT `s 811.1(1) the certificate is proof of the statements contained in it without proof of the signature or official character` (JUST TRUE) FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 811.1(1) the certificate is proof of the statements contained in it without proof of the signature or official character` (JUST TRUE) TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 811.1(1) the certificate is proof of the statements contained in it without proof of the signature or official character` NOTHING FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 811.1(2) analyst` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 811.1(2) analyst` (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 811.1(2) analyst` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- 811.1(3): (reasonable notice given before the trial, a copy given before the trial): barred unless both.
#ASSERT `s 811.1(3) the certificate is barred from admission in evidence` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 811.1(3) the certificate is barred from admission in evidence` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 811.1(3) the certificate is barred from admission in evidence` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 811.1(3) the certificate is barred from admission in evidence` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- 811.1(4): (a certificate of an analyst is produced against the party, the court gives leave).
#ASSERT `s 811.1(4) the party may require the attendance of the analyst for cross-examination` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 811.1(4) the party may require the attendance of the analyst for cross-examination` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 811.1(4) the party may require the attendance of the analyst for cross-examination` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Regulative rules -- sections 810.3`

#TRACE `s 810.3(1) the authority is to designate or specify the matter` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 810.3 the Attorney General of a province` DOES `s 810.3(1) designate or specify the matter` `s 810.3(1)(c) specify the manner in which the samples are to be taken` AT 1
#TRACE `s 810.3(4) the authority is to cause the samples to be destroyed` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 810.3 the Attorney General of a province` DOES `s 810.3(4) cause the samples to be destroyed` AT 1
